# asap-otel-supervised — the asap-otel collector wrapped by the OpenTelemetry
# opamp-supervisor so the agent APPLIES the config the controller pushes over
# OpAMP (instead of just reporting health like the bare opampextension does).
#
# ## Why a separate image
#
# The plain `asap/asap-otel:dev` image runs the collector directly and embeds
# the `opampextension`, which is REPORT-ONLY: it connects to the controller's
# OpAMP server and reports health + effective config, but it can NOT reload the
# collector or apply a pushed remote config. So the agent keeps running its
# static mounted config forever (controller logs "config pushed" while the
# agent reports remote-config status=Unset).
#
# The opamp-supervisor is the component that owns the collector process: it
# connects to the controller's OpAMP server, receives the AgentRemoteConfig,
# MERGES it with its own bootstrap pieces, writes the result to disk, and
# (re)starts the collector against it. This image runs the supervisor as the
# entrypoint and lets it spawn the asap-otel collector binary.
#
# ## Build model: host-build, container-ship (same as Dockerfile.asap-otel)
#
# 1. Build the asap-otel collector + the asap/asap-otel:dev image first
#    (see Dockerfile.asap-otel header). The supervisor needs the collector
#    binary at /usr/local/bin/asap-otel, which that image already provides.
#
# 2. Build the supervisor binary into the docker build context:
#
#      ./build_opamp_supervisor.sh
#        # → deploy/docker/opampsupervisor
#
# 3. Build this image (COPY below expects the supervisor binary present in the
#    build context):
#
#      docker build -f deploy/docker/Dockerfile.asap-otel-supervised \
#        -t asap/asap-otel-supervised:dev .
#
# The supervisor reads its OWN config (server endpoint, per-agent X-Agent-ID,
# capabilities, the collector executable path, storage dir) from a mounted
# supervisor.yaml — see deploy/mvp-multinode/configs/asap/supervisor.yaml.

# Start from the already-built collector image so the asap-otel binary +
# ca-certificates are present and stay in lockstep with the rest of the deploy.
FROM asap/asap-otel:dev

# Supervisor needs a writable storage dir for its instance UID / last remote
# config hash. run_demo mounts the supervisor.yaml at /etc/otel/supervisor.yaml
# and points storage.directory here.
RUN mkdir -p /etc/otel/supervisor-storage

COPY deploy/docker/opampsupervisor /usr/local/bin/opampsupervisor

# OTLP receivers (4317/4318) + self-telemetry (8888) + prometheus (9464) are
# served by the collector the supervisor spawns; the supervisor's local OpAMP
# server + health-check server bind loopback/ephemeral ports inside the
# container (host network in the deploy), so nothing extra to EXPOSE here.

# Supervisor is the entrypoint: it manages the asap-otel collector process and
# applies the controller's remote config. Override the base image's collector
# entrypoint/cmd.
ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/opampsupervisor"]
CMD ["--config", "/etc/otel/supervisor.yaml"]
